"description":
"This session includes in vivo recordings of reward- and movement-related dopamine, spikes, and local field potentials obtained using single- and dual-channel micro-invasive neural implants (s-µIPs) chronically implanted in the striatum of task-performing rhesus monkeys. Recordings were made during performance of reward-biased eye movement tasks, enabling simultaneous measurement of neurochemical and electrophysiological activity associated with behavior.",
